  "summary": "Minimalist REST API contract for task management delivered as a strictly valid JSON document. The contract defines the Task resource model (id, title, description, status) and standard CRUD endpoints (/tasks, /tasks/{id}) using standard HTTP methods (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE) and status codes (200, 201, 204). Contract JSON: {"resource":"Task","model":{"id":"string","title":"string","description":"string","status":"string (pending|in_progress|completed)"},"endpoints":[{"path":"/tasks","method":"GET","response":{"status":200,"body":"Task[]"}},{"path":"/tasks","method":"POST","request":{"body":{"title":"string","description":"string","status":"string"}},"response":{"status":201,"body":"Task"}},{"path":"/tasks/{id}","method":"GET","response":{"status":200,"body":"Task"}},{"path":"/tasks/{id}","method":"PUT","request":{"body":{"title":"string","description":"string","status":"string"}},"response":{"status":200,"body":"Task"}},{"path":"/tasks/{id}","method":"DELETE","response":{"status":204,"body":null}}]}",
  "approach": "Define a /tasks resource collection adhering to REST constraints. Implement standard HTTP methods: POST (create), GET (read all/read one), PUT (update), DELETE (remove). The Task model includes id (string/uuid), title (string), description (string), and status (enum: pending, in_progress, completed). The API contract is structured as a simplified JSON document mapping paths, methods, and payload schemas, avoiding full OpenAPI verbosity to maintain minimalism.",
  "tradeoffs": [
    "Simplified JSON vs OpenAPI: Using a custom simplified JSON reduces verbosity and complexity but sacrifices standard tooling compatibility (e.g., Swagger UI, code generators).",
    "Minimalist Scope: Excluding pagination, filtering, and detailed error codes keeps the design clean but may require API versioning or expansion for production-scale use cases."
  ],
  "evidence": [
    "REST architectural constraints (Fielding, 2000) dictate resource-based URIs and uniform interface methods, which this contract strictly follows.",
    "JSON is the de facto standard for REST API payloads, ensuring broad client compatibility without requiring XML parsing."
